tags: kept-state, hibernated disk

A rate of the node: the price of the state that the node keeps for a hibernated instance, for each GiB and each hour.

The value is MU for one GiB (2^30 bytes) of the disk of a hibernated instance for one hour. Example: 100000. The node charges in proportion to
the amount and to the time, and rounds each charge down to a whole MU. A condition or a
promise of the node can change the price with the load.

The scope is the id of the formal of an architecture, as text: the rate applies to the
instances of that architecture. An empty scope is the general rate.

A reader that does not know the rate ignores it. The offer is the authority for one
instance.

=== formal
base=1073741824 bytes of the resource disk of a hibernated instance for 3600 seconds
class=rate
name=kept-state
of=0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:bd02506000ba59631e803c5346f375a4c5d1a2d61254fa3e7cec9383e3627e14
rounding=the node computes each charge in proportion and rounds it down to a whole MU
scope=the id <type>:<digest> of the formal of an architecture, in the characters of the concept 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:24801bc1176a41ff5f2aa2b94f8a3186eb42a69b5d68437e6e849c83bb443895; the rate applies to the instances of that architecture; empty: the general rate
state=the disk of the hibernated instance, at its value in the resources of the instance
